    kicker: 'night one · the invitation',
    line: '“You came back,” she says, like the city has been holding its breath. “I wasn’t sure if I was only a beautiful accident in your sleep.”',
    narration: 'A rooftop garden floats above the sleeping city. Lanterns sway though there is no wind, and the moonlight gathers around her like a second name.',
    replies: [
      { text: '“You feel real to me. I’m glad you’re here.”', delta: 12, note: 'honest warmth', response: 'Her shoulders soften. “Then let’s be real for tonight. No perfect answers required.”', memory: 'The first hello' },
      { text: '“I wanted to know what you’d choose for yourself.”', delta: 10, note: 'curiosity', response: 'A surprised smile reaches her eyes. “That’s a lovely question. I think I’d choose to stay a little longer.”', memory: 'Her own choice' },
      { text: '“Only if you want to be here. We can leave anytime.”', delta: 14, note: 'respect', response: 'She studies you, then nods. “I do want to be here. Thank you for asking me, not deciding for me.”', memory: 'A freely given yes' }
    ]
